  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.2. Increased institutional capacity of workers&#x2019; organizations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Timor-Leste Trade Union Confederation (KSTL) established Centro De Forma&#xE7;&#xE3;o Sindical E Aperfei&#xE7;oamento Profissional/ Trade Union Training and Professional Improvement Centre (CEFOSAP) in 2022 and upon its establishment submitted proposals to the Secretariat of State for Vocational Training on Employment (SEFOPE) for budget support and certification process of the training centre from National Institute of Manpower Development (INDMO) so that better service provision could be provided. The proposals were considered, and the Center is now able to provide various skills development for union members and increase their capacity on soft skills, negotiations and labour rights while engaging in various vocational training activities. Around 500 youth workers have been trained by CEFOSAP. The ILO provided support to KSTL for the operationalisation of the training centre CEFOSAP. The ILO also supported KSTL in the development of a proposal to the Secretariat of State for Vocational Training on Employment (SEFOPE) for budget support and certification process of the training centre from the National Institute of Manpower Development (INDMO) so that better service provision could be provided.</narrative>
   </description>
